WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.067
In 1834,

2
00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:04.567
Britain’s Parliament
caught fire

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.833
because workers were
destroying old receipts.

4
00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:10.133
The receipts were
wooden sticks.

5
00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:12.300
For centuries,

6
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.633
the government recorded
payments with notches,

7
00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.500
then split the wood

8
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:20.400
so both sides kept
a matching record.

9
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.467
When that system
became obsolete,

10
00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:27.033
two cartloads of sticks
were left to dispose of.

11
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:30.533
Workers fed them
into heating furnaces

12
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.833
beneath the House of Lords.

13
00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.400
A chimney fire smouldered

14
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:37.433
under the chamber floor.

15
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.733
Heat and smoke
were noticed,

16
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:41.933
but the burning continued.

17
00:00:42.433 --> 00:00:44.967
That evening,
flames broke through.

18
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.633
Both parliamentary chambers
were destroyed.

19
00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.067
Westminster Hall survived.

20
00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.733
The dangerous part wasn’t

21
00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.967
keeping records on wood.

22
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.367
It was choosing
where to burn them.
